Prompt: what is the default for supabase
Response: Supabase Auth uses the following default values:

Access Token (JWT) Expiration: 3,600 seconds (1 hour). Every request sent with this token is valid for 1 hour from issuance.

Auto Refresh Lead Time: The Supabase client library automatically triggers a background refresh 60 seconds before the 1-hour access token expires.

Overall Session & Refresh Token Lifetime: Indefinite (no time limit) on the default/free tier. A user will remain signed in indefinitely as long as their client continues to auto-refresh and they do not manually log out.

Refresh Token Reuse Interval: 10 seconds. If multiple simultaneous requests try to use the same refresh token within a 10-second window, Supabase permits it rather than instantly revoking the session.

Where to View or Adjust This:
In your Supabase Dashboard:

Go to Authentication → Configuration (or Settings → Auth).

Look under Sessions or JWT Expiry.

You will see JWT expiry limit set to 3600 seconds.

